+        -----
+
+        **Input datasets**
+
+        Multiple `quant.sf` files may be selected at once; a list collection of `quant.sf`
+        files (for example the output of a Salmon quant step run on a collection of samples)
+        can be handed to the input as well, in which case a single merged TPM, NumReads or
+        length matrix is produced.
+
+        The column headers of the merged matrix are derived from the dataset identifiers;
+        every character that is not a letter, a digit, an underscore or a hyphen is replaced
+        by `_`. Names beginning with a hyphen are prefixed with `_`. If names collide
+        after this conversion, numeric suffixes (`_2`, `_3`, ...) make them unique,
+        preserving the names of other inputs and the input order.
+
+        Enable **Gene-level input files** when the inputs contain gene-level quantifications (`quant.genes.sf`).
+        This option does not aggregate transcript-level quantifications into genes.
